  "主要内容": "The semiconductor industry experienced a record year in 2015 with M&A deals totaling over USD 120 billion. Companies increased scale to meet customer demands, driven by rising manufacturing costs and fixed chip development expenses. Key deals included Avago's acquisition of Broadcom, Qualcomm's purchase of CSR, Intel's acquisition of Altera, NXP's takeover of Freescale, Dialog's acquisition of Atmel, and Western Digital's purchase of SanDisk. The semiconductor industry experienced a record year in M&A activity in 2015, with North American and Chinese firms leading the trend. U.S. companies such as Intel Corporation, Broadcom Corporation, Qualcomm Incorporated, Avago Technologies Ltd, Micron Technology, Inc., and Samsung Electronics Co., Ltd were highly active. China also bolstered its semiconductor acquisitions through aggressive M&A. Key strategies included partnerships, agreements, contracts, mergers, and new product developments.",
